 a
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/ilac-de-las-fosas-comunes-al-
 espacio-publico-la-memoria-de-la-guerra-civil-y-el-franquismo-en-catalunya
 -y-espana\n\nQueralt Solé i Barjau is Associate Professor in the Departme
 nt of History and Archaeology at the University of Barcelona and this year
 ’s Josep Pla visiting chair in Catalan Studies at the DLCL. She has a Ph
 D in Contemporary History from the University of Barcelona. She is the aut
 hor of eleven books and eight editions on the history of the repression du
 ring and after the Spanish Civil War\, a field in which she counts among t
 he foremost specialists.\n\n“From Mass Graves to Public Space: The Memor
 y of the Civil War and Francoism in Catalonia and Spain”\n\n25 years sin
 ce Franco’s death had to pass and mass graves be reopened before the mem
 ory of the losers in the Civil War could be vindicated\, while the memory 
 of the Franco regime remained alive in public space. Against this backgrou
 nd\, memory has become a political\, cultural\, and social battlefield\, a
 s the memorial landscape shifts in Spain and especially in Catalonia. The 
 emergence of new social agents\, memorialist associations\, researchers an
 d relatives of the victims has called into question the dominant narrative
 s and promoted new demands. In this way\, the memory of twentieth-century 
 political violence in Spain has claimed an ever more relevant place in the
  public debate and contemporary political identities\, encouraging the tra
 nsformation of memorial space through the modification\, elimination or in
 corporation of monuments\, sculptures\, plaques\, memorials and other symb
 ols in public space.\n\nThis talk will be in Spanish.
